@startuml
title CSP identity assignment on abstract seed graph (backtracking + MRV + AC-3)

start
:Initialize domain(node) = all identities\ncompatible with fixed boundary edges,\nfor every unassigned node;
:Run AC-3 once up front\n(propagate fixed-boundary constraints\ninto neighboring domains before any guess);

if (any domain emptied by initial AC-3?) then (yes)
  :Report failure to caller -\nnothing assigned yet, this triggers\nthe outer reseed, not backtracking;
  stop
else (no)
endif

while (unassigned nodes remain?) is (yes)
  :Select node with fewest remaining\ndomain values (MRV);

  if (domain has an untried identity?) then (yes)
    :Pick next untried identity;
    :Tentatively assign;
    :AC-3 - prune neighbors' domains\nof now-incompatible identities;
    if (any neighbor domain emptied?) then (yes)
      :Undo assignment and every\npruning it caused;
      :Mark identity tried, discard;
    else (no)
      :Commit assignment,\nadvance to next node;
    endif
  else (no)
    if (a previous decision exists\nto backtrack to?) then (yes)
      :Undo that earlier node's assignment\nand its AC-3 pruning;
      :Resume there, try its\nnext untried identity;
    else (no)
      :No assignment possible from\nthis graph - report failure to caller;
      stop
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no)
:All nodes assigned - success;
stop

note right
  Deliberately adjacency-only, no size check here — matches
  fix_dieas.md's own Step 2 formulation (variables = nodes,
  domain = identities, constraint = adjacency legality per
  edge). A per-node "does this identity's size class fit"
  gate would need a real area estimate (Voronoi-cell area),
  which doesn't exist until Step 3 realizes geometry - a
  fuzzy pre-geometry proxy isn't worth building. Step 3
  (geometry-realization.puml) can still come up short of an
  assigned identity's true min_size; that's what local
  repair downstream exists to catch, not this stage.
end note
@enduml
